codemap 8
path behaviour-pin
kind layer
author ai
group tests
note How a change proves what it did to the tool's behaviour. The harness lives in crates/codemap/tests: common/ holds the fixture, the runners and every scenario; cli.rs and gui.rs turn the scenario lists into one #[test] each, parity.rs plays them against two builds, and features.rs checks the feature registry against the map and the goldens. cargo test replays every CLI command against a generated fixture repo and compares golden transcripts, and plays scripted GUI scenarios in real windows and compares the state after each step. A change that means to alter output reblesses the goldens (CODEMAP_BLESS=1) and the golden diff is the evidence; a refactor instead runs the parity test, which plays every scenario with the old build and the new one and compares transcripts, GUI dumps and screenshots byte for byte. Every run sees a PATH with jj and git and no language server, so every file is indexed by tree-sitter and the output is the same on every run; a scenario that needs jj or git skips itself, with the reason on stderr, when that tool is not installed.

